-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Smooth Z-Buffer Instability:** Pixels not covered by any triangle may appear to have visible triangles because low weights close to zero can cause high values in the weighted SoftMin [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Stabilization:** To stabilize this, two triangles covering the background are added, and the visibility value is reduced with increasing distance from triangles [S1, unofficial].
+**Stabilization of Smooth Z-Buffer:**
+The smooth z-buffer used in the Soft Rasterizer can cause pixels not covered by any triangle to appear as if they have visible triangles because low weights close to zero can cause high values in the weighted SoftMin. To stabilize this, two triangles covering the background are added, and the visibility value is reduced with increasing distance from triangles [S1, unofficial].
 
